-- **Database:** new licence tables with RLS deny-all for client roles. All writes go through `SECURITY DEFINER` RPCs. Each RPC first checks `is_platform_admin()`, and if decision 14 is yes, `auth.jwt()->>'aal' = 'aal2'`. Each RPC writes its audit row in the same transaction. `EXECUTE` is revoked from `public`, `anon`, `authenticated`, and `service_role` on internal helpers. Migration 0011 also revokes all table privileges from the same four roles. The `service_role` revocation is a migration choice that differs from 0010; owner review pending (recorded 2026-11-01). Admin RPCs are granted to `authenticated` only, and each checks admin status and aal2 itself. *Corrected 2026-10-29 (R9, §12B.5).*
