 ### 12A.6 Access states and precedence
 
-A coverage record `c` is effective at time `t` if `c.starts_at <= t`, `t < c.ends_at` (or it has no end, for lifetime), and `t < c.revoked_at` (if revoked). Intervals are half-open: at exactly `ends_at` or `revoked_at`, the coverage is no longer effective.
+A coverage record `c` is effective at time `t` if `c.starts_at <= t`, `t < c.ends_at` (or it has no end, for lifetime), and `t < c.revoked_at` (if revoked). Intervals are half-open: at exactly `ends_at` or `revoked_at`, the coverage is no longer effective. Owner-facing reads evaluate `t` at the current time only; historical state queries are not supported (owner decision 11, 2026-11-01). History comes from `licence_audit_log`.
 
 **Access** is granted if any coverage is effective at `t`. Overlaps are allowed and do not add time.
 
 *Corrected 2026-10-29 (state-machine fixes 1–11, §12B.5).* The **state** is chosen in this order. The first match wins. Only ACTIVE grants access.
 
-1. **ACTIVE:** an effective coverage contains `t`. **Basis** describes current access only: the highest-ranked effective kind (`lifetime_grant`, then `admin_grant`; `paid_verified` is deferred, M5). The ranking was confirmed by the owner on 2026-11-01 (item 7). `access_until` is the end of the contiguous block that contains `t` (algorithm in §12B.5). Lifetime gives no expiry. *The next start shown in ACTIVE is OPEN: no owner decision exists. Migration 0011 returns NULL outside SCHEDULED.*
